SUMMARY:Play-Based Music & Movement for Little Ones (Caregiver + Child Class)
DESCRIPTION:Join me for a play-based music and movement class for young children and their caregivers. I’m a music educator with over 20 years of experience working with children\, and I love creating spaces where kids can explore music in a way that feels natural\, joyful\, and developmentally right for them. \nIn each class\, we’ll focus on things like steady beat\, rhythm\, singing\, and creative movement through games\, songs\, and simple musical play. Everything is designed so caregivers can participate right alongside their child and build connection through music! \nWhile the class is playful and fun\, it’s also intentionally structured using approaches rooted in early childhood music education (including Orff-inspired practices)\, so children are building real musical foundations as they play. \nThis class is a great fit for toddlers and preschool-aged children who love to move\, sing\, and explore sound in a relaxed\, welcoming environment. Drop-in option available for $25/class.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/play-based-music-movement-for-little-ones-caregiver-child-class/2026-05-05/
LOCATION:Steady Beat Music Studio\, 14629 SE Poppy Hills Dr\, Happy Valley\, OR\, 97086\, United States
